--TEST--
A `Core\Db\Connection` that a child task returns names no connection in the task that receives it, so a statement on it there stops the program and never reaches the task's own connection at the same position — `rule:core-classes/db-connection-is-named`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Db::connect
// A task returns a connection, and a statement on it outside the task stops the program.
// Before that, the program's own connection reads its own table.

var $own = Core\Db::connect("main");
$own->execute("create table own (name text)", []);
$own->execute("insert into own (name) values (?)", ["own row"]);

var $result = Core\Task::all({
    db: fn (): Core\Db\Connection => Core\Db::connect("main"),
});
echo "own rows: ", $own->query("select name from own", [])->count(), "\n";
$result->db->query("select name from own", []);
echo "this line does not run\n";
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.db]
connect = ["main"]

[db.main]
driver = "sqlite"
path = ":memory:"
--EXPECT--
own rows: 1
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
FATAL: `Core\Db\Connection::query` was called on a connection from another task. A connection works only in the task that called `Core\Db::connect`.
